WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:04.350
Gus Fring, is one of the most 
iconic villains in TV history,

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:06.770
with his monster 
methamphetamine empire

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:09.340
run under the front 
of Los Pollos Hermanos,

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:10.620
a local favorite.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:12.830
In Breaking Bad, 
Jessie would reveal that

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:16.380
Gus could be pulling upwards of 
$96 million in revenue

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:18.070
over a three-month period.

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:20.240
But this was after 
decades of growth

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.300
and only lasted 
a few months.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.150
So, how much money 
did Gus Fring,

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:25.960
make over his entire career?

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:31.140
? Trailer Sport Action Motivational -
by Romansenykmusic ?

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:32.510
Well, starting off,

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:34.360
let's take a look at 
his legal business,

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:36.080
Los Pollos Hermanos.

00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:39.400
Similar businesses generally pull in 
a few million dollars in revenue

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:40.850
per store per year.

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:44.260
For example, KFC 
has hovered in the 900's

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:46.430
for much of the past 15 years.

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:48.130
Chick-fil-A on the other hand,

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:50.940
rakes in over $4 million 
per store annually.

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:55.330
One of the main reasons that KFC has 
significantly lower revenue numbers is that,

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:59.120
KFC, like many other fast-food 
chains, has overextended,

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:02.860
leading to more restaurants with 
lower revenue per restaurant.

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:05.960
Given that, Los Pollos Hermanos 
is an up-and-coming brand

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:08.630
that has been quickly 
expanding up to 14 stores,

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:12.570
It's safe to assume that they're generating 
1-2 million dollars in revenue annually,

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:13.570
per store.

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:16.570
Let's just say $1 million each, 
to be conservative,

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:20.460
which would mean $14 million 
in revenue from Los Pollos Hermanos.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:23.460
Gus has been in business 
for about 20 years.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:27.390
And, let's assume that the majority 
of the profits made in the first 15 years

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:29.330
were reinvested into business

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:32.560
adding locations, trucks, marketing, 
and so on and so forth.

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:36.090
As a result, we will say that 
Los Pollos Hermanos

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:37.830
has been a stable 
regional chain

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:39.550
for about five years.

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:42.950
The average restaurant 
profit margin is 3 to 5%.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:45.520
So, assuming a 4% profit margin,

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:47.220
Los Pollos Hermanos

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:51.270
would have generated 
$560,000 in profits per year,

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:53.780
or $2.8 million over five years.

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:56.520
And, we can use 
this figure to estimate

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:59.970
the total valuation of the business 
including all of its assets.

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:01.830
During this time period,

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:04.230
the average P/E ratio 
for restaurant chains

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:06.200
was about ten to fifteen.

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:08.020
This is based on the P/E ratio

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:09.850
of Yum Brands during the time period,

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:13.610
who owns a variety of restaurants, 
including KFC, Taco Bell, and PizzaHut.

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:17.310
The P/E ratio, 
or Price to Earnings ratio

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:21.380
is just a ratio between a company's 
yearly earnings, and its valuation.

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:23.360
As Los Pollos Hermanos makes

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:26.240
$560,000 in profits per year,

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:28.780
with the p/e ratio of 12.5,

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:31.850
Los Pollos Hermanos could be 
worth $7 million.

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:34.440
But this is not all Gus's.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:35.740
It is clear that Madrigal

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:39.150
has some sort of significant 
ownership in Los Pollos Hermanos.

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:42.300
Some people suggest that 
it is the parent company,

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:45.290
while others insist that Gus 
is still majority owner.

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:46.500
So, we'll just say that

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:48.850
Gus and Madrigal 
are 50/50 owners.

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:52.000
Given all of this, 
over Gus's career,

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:53.970
Los Pollos Hermanos 
has given him

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:56.280
$3.5 million in net worth,

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.700
and about $1.4 million
in income,

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:00.700
or about $5 million 
in total.

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:04.130
Moving on, let's take a look 
at his drug empire,

00:03:04.130 --> 00:03:06.470
most of which, 
was with the cartel.

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:08.970
Badger tells Jesse, that 
street grade meth

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:12.330
has a market price of about 
$1700 per ounce

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:15.000
or about $27,200 per pound.

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:17.580
When Walter was cooking for Gus,

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:20.190
we know that Gus was moving 
200 pounds per week.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:24.050
But this was after Gus took over
 Hector Salamanca's territory.

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:27.940
So, originally, when he was 
working under Juan Bolsa,

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:31.150
let's say that he was handling, 
on average, 100 pounds per week.

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:35.390
First of all, out of his revenue, 
Gus would have to pay the cartel,

00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:37.510
who handles the production 
of the substance.

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:39.560
Let's say, their cut is 30%.

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:41.540
Next, we have the Mules

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:43.820
working across Gus's 
distribution network,

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:45.700
getting the products 
to the dealers.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:48.090
Mike reveals that 
their pay is 20%.

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:50.780
Let's also say, that 
the dealers cut is 20%.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:55.510
Finally, let's say Mike and Gus's 
other right hand men, get 10%.

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:57.510
This sounds low.

00:03:57.510 --> 00:03:59.510
But you have to remember that 10%

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:01.790
is split among just 
a handful of people,

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:04.090
as opposed to the 20 or 30%,

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:06.370
which is split between 
hundreds of people.

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:09.770
This finally leaves Gus, 
with 20% of the revenue.

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:14.050
This makes sense, as it would assume 
the cartel makes the largest portion,

00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:17.860
followed up by Gus, who is taking on 
the risk of a distribution network.

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:20.350
So, with 100 pounds per week,

00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:23.780
Gus would have been making 
$544,000 per week

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:26.330
or about $2.2 million per month

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:28.030
and $28 million per year.

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:30.370
With 20 years in the business,

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:33.250
this would add up to $565 million.

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:36.320
We knew that Gus lived 
well below his means

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:38.700
driving old Volvo, and owning 
a modest house.

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:43.770
We can assume, that his living expenses were 
well under his Los Pollos Hermanos income.

00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:45.350
So, all of this drug money

00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:46.750
was just pure net worth.

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:49.540
Let's just take off another $65 million

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:51.970
or about 11% as unexpected issues.

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:56.430
Maybe they had production issues, 
or they had to scale back for a little bit.

00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:58.880
Anyways, before Walter, 
and the lab,

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:02.180
Gus had made at least $500 million
from the drug trade.

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:04.950
The math is pretty much 
the same after Walt enters,

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:06.450
with just a few differences.

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:09.610
Gus no longer has to pay 
the cartel 30%

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:11.460
as he has his own 
production means.

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:13.670
He now also controls 
Hector's territory

00:05:13.670 --> 00:05:15.500
leading to 200 pounds 
per week,

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:17.580
and the meth itself 
now sells for

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:19.190
$2,500 per ounce.

00:05:19.730 --> 00:05:21.030
Instead of the cartel,

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:24.260
Gus has to pay Lydia and Chao, 
20%, for the chemicals,

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:26.970
and Walter and Jesse 
$1 million per month.

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:29.030
The amount he pays 
Walter and Jesse,

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:32.390
works out to about 3.9%, 
even with the upgrade

00:05:32.390 --> 00:05:34.140
of $15 million a year.

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:35.810
Let's just call them 5%.

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:38.830
And then, of course, 
there is the cost of the lab,

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:40.990
which is estimated 
to be $8 million

00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:42.270
but, let's just call it ten.

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:45.030
However, that's just 
a one-time cost.

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:49.570
So, overall, Gus's profit margin 
increases to about 25%.

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:52.600
So, Gus isn't really making 
all that much more

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:53.610
in terms of percent,

00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:55.970
compared to when he was 
working with the cartel.

00:05:55.970 --> 00:05:58.890
But the key difference, is that 
he now has full control

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:00.370
and has a higher market price.

00:06:00.950 --> 00:06:03.920
Given that this setup continues 
for about six months,

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:05.930
Gus would roughly make $52 million

00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:07.060
over that time period.

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:09.780
So, at the time of Gus's death,

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:12.460
he was making about 
$100 million per year

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:14.460
But as he dies,

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:16.540
he only gets to about $50 million

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:18.370
minus the $10 million lab cost.

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:21.110
This means that Gus 
conservatively made

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:24.100
a total of $540 million 
from his empire.

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:26.950
Combined with Los Pollos Hermanos,

00:06:26.950 --> 00:06:30.880
Gus was worth about $545 million 
at the time of his death.

00:06:31.350 --> 00:06:32.870
But, that's just conservative.

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:36.150
Gus may have been peddling 
200 pounds the entire time,

00:06:36.690 --> 00:06:38.130
and his restaurant chain

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:41.170
may very well be worth double 
what we originally estimated.

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:45.700
So, Gus could be worth 
up to $1.05 billion.

00:06:46.310 --> 00:06:47.850
The real number however,

00:06:47.850 --> 00:06:49.620
was probably right in the middle

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:51.750
at $795 million.

00:06:52.150 --> 00:06:53.900
Or, about $800 million

00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:55.550
plus or minus $100 million.

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:59.010
So, unfortunately, Gus, 
likely never reached

00:06:59.010 --> 00:07:01.280
a billion dollar mark, 
in terms of net worth.

00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:03.760
But, his drug business 
would have been worth

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:05.390
1 to 2 billion dollars

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:07.090
given his yearly income.

00:07:07.090 --> 00:07:09.360
However, you can't really 
sell this business

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:12.110
to Apple or Google, given, 
the nature of their business.

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:14.620
So, that figure is 
basically meaningless,

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:16.460
and wouldn't add on 
to his net worth.

00:07:16.780 --> 00:07:19.740
But, hey, Gus did run 
a unicorn meth Empire.

00:07:20.260 --> 00:07:25.040
However, as Jesse said, "&lt;i&gt;Is a meth Empire 
really something to be that proud of".&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:26.190 --> 00:07:28.540
And, given that Gus lived so modestly,

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:31.240
maybe he should have just 
stuck to Los Pollos Hermanos

00:07:31.240 --> 00:07:33.570
as he would have lived 
a much longer life

00:07:33.570 --> 00:07:35.130
and wouldn't have worked so hard,

00:07:35.130 --> 00:07:37.490
just to end up giving it all, 
to Uncle Sam.

